# <%= it.scope.slice(1) %>-shell

The shell of a polyrepo made with [mfeflow](https://github.com/mfeflow/mfeflow): routes, layout and
the registry that tells it which build of each remote to load. The remotes are in their own repos.

```
apps/shell                                  the host
apps/shell/public/config/runtime-config.*   per environment; dev lists where the remotes run
registry/envs                               which build of each remote staging and prod serve
```

## Run it

```sh
pnpm install
pnpm dev
```

`pnpm dev` starts the shell on http://localhost:4300. It finds each remote in `devRemotes` in
`apps/shell/public/config/runtime-config.dev.json`. Start a remote with `pnpm dev` in its own repo.

`pnpm mfeflow dev` runs the shell the same way and reloads the list when that file changes.
Point one remote somewhere else for a run with `pnpm mfeflow dev --remote cart=http://localhost:3001`.

## Add a team repo

```sh
pnpm mfeflow add team-repo checkout
```

This creates `../checkout` as a new git repo and registers it here. Run `git init` and the GitHub
steps yourself.
